hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-20 = unlines (cons "The earth, from which the human is named (*humus*, *adamah*), teaches by text. *Text* comes from *texere*, to weave, and so do *textile* and *context*. The Greek *tekhnē*, craft, from which *technology* comes, goes back to the same Indo-European root for weaving and building. So technology and text are one family: both are weaving. DNA is a text in the literal sense, a woven strand. An interaction net is woven. A network is net + work. The web is a web. The words never stopped saying that information is woven, and that weaving is how the given gets its shape." nil)
